  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Waving at You** (1 review): The source singles out this specific track as the standout performance of the night [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Harlem Roulette**: back after 45 archived shows (1422 days) [4]\n- **Psalms 40:2**: back after 55 archived shows (1596 days) [4]\n- **Isaiah 45:23**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **Weekend in Western Illinois**: back after 28 archived shows (828 days); rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Waving at You**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Fire Editorial**: rare: 6 archived performances [4]\n- **California Jam**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **Letter From Belgium**: back after 74 archived shows (2352 days) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2016-09-18.RamsHead** (recommended): source not stated; 22 songs; 90 min; rated 3/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Phone recording struggles with bass drum, though banter and other tracks remain solid; Bass drum sounds like a Tom Waits song due to the phone recording quality [2][3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: California Jam, Elijah, Foreign Editorial, Foreign Object, Waving at You [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2016-09-18.RamsHead**: taped by The Empty Stage [1]. Also: Recorded on a phone by the uploader, who prioritized enjoying the show over preservation [1]",
